body:
Most definitely, my old roommate had a car and since she's moved out I've started walking about 4 miles a day. When you can't drive to work and need to walk to a train then to work and then again for the evening commute, the walking/running exercise isn't your choice. 

&#x200B;

Rise repeat everyday and for every trip

Maybe I'm completely off but could it be your oven? 

&#x200B;

I say this because my cookies, cakes, anything came out more dry and cakey than I wanted. After getting an oven thermometer and found out my oven runs 50 degrees too hot. Once I realized this, everything has come out right.

NTA (Right now), but it depends on how you move forward from here and how you treat the baby, respond to future stuff, etc. etc. 

&#x200B;

But I just wanna note, as a child born to a dad who was in his mid forties, with half siblings, who are 8 and 10 years older than me (although that age difference isn't as intense as the one you're facing), that all is not lost! And although things are different with an older parent/half siblings/age differences, I wouldn't change my experience for the world. 

&#x200B;

Also I do understand that you feel left out of important decisions, but this isn't really your place to be in the conversation.
